# 18. TICK-SIZE ROUNDING

The exchange market defines:

```text
tick_size
step_size
min_order_size
max_order_size
```

The bot MUST respect these constraints.

Before submitting an order:

```text
calculate price
      ↓
round to tick size
      ↓
validate
      ↓
calculate quantity
      ↓
round to step size
      ↓
validate
      ↓
submit
```

Never send arbitrary floating-point precision to the exchange.

Prefer decimal-safe arithmetic.

Avoid relying on naive JavaScript floating-point calculations for financial values when precision matters.

If the existing exchange API represents financial values as strings, preserve that convention.

