# 26. IDEMPOTENCY

The bot must protect against duplicate order creation.

If a request times out, do NOT blindly assume the order failed.

Possible situation:

```text
Bot → Exchange
       │
       │ order created
       ▼
Exchange
       X
network response lost
       │
       ▼
Bot sees timeout
```

If the bot blindly retries:

```text
order A created
order B created
```

you may accidentally create duplicate liquidity.

The order manager should reconcile with the exchange's actual open-order state before blindly retrying ambiguous order creation.

Use the exchange's existing idempotency/client-order-ID mechanism if available.

