calculate new quotes
      ↓
place replacement liquidity
```

Do not assume that a resting order remains forever.

---

# 45. TRADE ACTIVITY IS THE GOAL

The service exists to produce realistic exchange activity.

Desired behavior:

```text
Binance price moves
        ↓
Bot quotes change
        ↓
Users see liquidity
        ↓
Users place orders
        ↓
Orders match
        ↓
Trades occur
        ↓
Positions update
        ↓
Balances update
        ↓
Order book continues moving
```

The bot should not attempt to manufacture fake fills against itself.

Its purpose is to provide liquidity that other exchange users can interact with.

---

# 46. IMPORTANT: NO SELF-TRADING

The bot should place resting bid/ask orders around the reference price.

It must NOT intentionally cross its own orders.

Do not implement:

```text
bot buys its own sell
```

or:

```text
bot sells into its own bid
```

The bot should provide liquidity, not generate meaningless self-trades.

---

# 47. SIMPLE QUOTING MODEL

For v1, use:

```text
Reference Price = Binance price

Bid = Reference Price - configured spread

Ask = Reference Price + configured spread
```

Then:

```text
round bid to tick size
round ask to tick size
```

and validate:

```text
bid < ask
```

If rounding causes:

```text
bid >= ask
```

do not place orders.

Recalculate using safe spacing.

---

